[Music]  27 years  [Music]  [Applause]  15 majors  and five back surgeries after turning  pro  [Applause]  the world's most popular golfer is now  the newest member of the three comma  club  when tiger's in town there's always a  crowd  [Music]  triumph  injury  scandal  failure and triumph again have filled  the years since tiger woods first  stalked the fairways at the 1997 masters  but through it all the 46 year old woods  has maintained his supremacy as one of  the top earning athletes in the world  raking in over 1.7 billion dollars in  salary endorsements and other income  over the course of his 27-year career  more than anyone else we've tracked  forbes now estimates his net worth to be  at least one billion dollars making him  one of just two active athletes to  achieve billionaire status along with  nba superstar lebron james michael  jordan the only other athlete  billionaire didn't hit 10 digits until  after he retired thanks to a well-timed  investment in the nba's charlotte  hornets less than 10 percent of wood's  career earnings and net worth come from  golf winnings he amassed his fortune  primarily through enormous endorsement  deals with brands like nike gatorade and  rolex he's also assembled an impressive  real estate portfolio including jupiter  florida and owns chunks of businesses  such as a restaurant called the woods  and an operator of upscale mini golf  courses with plans to expand nationwide  the center of attention even on the  practice range tiger woods preparing for  his second round with all the meticulous  attention to detail which has turned him  into what many believe is the best  player the world has ever seen woods's  impact on golf's tv ratings and purse  sizes cannot be overstated ten thousand  fans came to watch this year's  three-time major winner tame the green  at hyde park in the early 2000s  according to former cbs president neil  pilsen tv audiences would drop 30 to 50  percent when woods was not in contention  at a tournament this so-called tiger  effect contributed to pga tour winnings  nearly tripling between 1996 and 2008 a  stretch in which woods won 14 major  championships and that's helped the  off-field bucks get much bigger too  there's a long tradition spanning babe  ruth to arnold palmer to jordan of  athletes getting paid to endorse brands  but now the endorsement potential  stretches into the three commas thanks  to the amplifying effect of modern media  and technology  woods for example has over 10 million  followers across twitter instagram and  other social media platforms at his peak  woods was the most prolific athlete  endorser in history earning north of 100  million dollars per year off the course  he held the number one spot in forbes  highest paid athletes list for 10  consecutive years ending in 2012. even  now despite hardly ever teeing the ball  up over the past 12 months while  recovering from a serious car accident  woods collected 68 million dollars in  off-course income  enough to make him the 14th highest paid  athlete in the world  woods has used his status and earnings  to expand his business which now  includes a golf design business a live  events production company and a  restaurant  woods is also identified as a partner in  a spack announced in january  when combined with his real estate  holdings woods's wealth is secured  whether or not he ever swings a golf  club again  [Music]  you

